  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a user messaging package for Laravel applications. This package aims to seamlessly integrate messaging or chat functionality into Laravel-based projects, facilitating communication between users within the application.\n\nObjectives\n\n- Develop a comprehensive user messaging system for Laravel applications.\n- Enable various messaging modes, including open threads, group messaging, and one-to-one messaging.\n- Offer optional features such as adding additional users to conversations and retrieving message statistics.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Developers: Implement the package into Laravel applications and customize for specific needs.\n- End Users: Engage in messaging through open threads, group messages, or private conversations.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Conversations Management\n   - Support multiple conversations per user.\n   - Enable optional inclusion of additional users in conversations.\n\n2. Message Viewing\n   - Display the last message in each thread.\n   - Return messages based on different criteria: all messages, user-specific messages, or new/unread messages.\n\n3. Unread Message Tracking\n   - Easily retrieve the count of unread messages for a user.\n\n4. Access Control\n   - Provide flexibility for implementing custom access control mechanisms.\n\n5. Messaging Modes\n   - Open Threads: Accessible by all users.\n   - Group Messaging: Restricted to thread participants.\n   - One-to-One Messaging: Private between two users.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Efficiently handle a large number of conversations and users.\n- Flexibility: Allow easy customization of access control and messaging features.\n- Ease of Integration: Ensure smooth integration into existing Laravel projects with minimal configuration.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0061\n\nCREATE TABLE `threads` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `subject` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open',\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `deleted_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `email` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `messages` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `thread_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `deleted_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `thread_id` (`thread_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `messages_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`thread_id`) REFERENCES `threads` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `messages_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `participants` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `thread_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `last_read` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `deleted_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `thread_id` (`thread_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `participants_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`thread_id`) REFERENCES `threads` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `participants_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
